From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diogo Trindade <diogotr7@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:18:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] media: iris: send the stream's POC type to the firmware

The firmware raises a source change when a stream property differs from
what the driver set. HFI_PROP_PIC_ORDER_CNT_TYPE is always set to 0, so
an H.264 stream of another type raises the same change again every time
the bitstream port is restarted. Set the type the firmware reported.

Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/b031deef99a095104ef234c5a0705850152dffe1/packages/kernel/patches/1030-media-iris-send-the-stream-POC-type.patch
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
index b071980ddd27..5901fbaffb8e 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -339,7 +339,7 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen2_set_picture_order_count(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 pla
 {
 	struct iris_inst_hfi_gen2 *inst_hfi_gen2 = to_iris_inst_hfi_gen2(inst);
 	u32 port = iris_hfi_gen2_get_port(inst, plane);
-	u32 poc = 0;
+	u32 poc = inst->fw_caps[POC].value;
 
 	inst_hfi_gen2->src_subcr_params.pic_order_cnt = poc;
 
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diogo Trindade <diogotr7@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:18:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] media: iris: stop the AV1 tier overwriting the HEVC tier

The TIER_AV1 capability has a setter that runs for every codec and
writes HFI_PROP_TIER to the bitstream port after
iris_hfi_gen2_set_tier(), so a High tier HEVC stream never matches and
raises the same source change on every restart. Drop the setter:
iris_hfi_gen2_set_tier() already sets the AV1 tier.

Link: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/b031deef99a095104ef234c5a0705850152dffe1/packages/kernel/patches/1031-media-iris-stop-AV1-tier-overwriting-HEVC-tier.patch
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
index 79bbd06ef8d2..dedb744f9a1f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2.c
@@ -1007,7 +1007,6 @@ static const struct platform_inst_fw_cap inst_fw_cap_sm8550_dec[] = {
 		.value = 0,
 		.hfi_id = HFI_PROP_TIER,
 		.flags = CAP_FLAG_INPUT_PORT,
-		.set = iris_set_u32,
 	},
 	{
 		.cap_id = DRAP,
